# Requests for the VS Code REST Client extension (humao.rest-client).
# Against `dotnet run` use 5080; against the Podman pod use 8081 (or 8080 through nginx).
@base = http://localhost:5080/api

### Health
GET {{base}}/health

### Settings
GET {{base}}/settings

### Quick add a task for today
POST {{base}}/tasks/quick-add
Content-Type: application/json

{ "text": "Review AG failover #origination !1", "today": true }

### Today's tasks
GET {{base}}/tasks/today

### Start a timer on task 1
POST {{base}}/timer/start
Content-Type: application/json

{ "taskId": 1 }

### Timer state (running entry, warnings, open interruption, pinned tasks)
GET {{base}}/timer

### Interrupted (pauses the timer)
POST {{base}}/interruptions/start
Content-Type: application/json

{ "sourceType": "WalkUp", "personName": "Dana", "note": "Access question" }

### Back to work (resumes the paused task)
POST {{base}}/interruptions/1/resume
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Convert an interruption into a task with its time
POST {{base}}/interruptions/1/convert
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": null, "projectId": 5, "status": "Done" }

### Daily review (today when date is omitted)
GET {{base}}/review

### Fill a gap
POST {{base}}/time-entries/fill-gap
Content-Type: application/json

{ "start": "2026-11-17T13:45:00Z", "end": "2026-11-17T14:30:00Z", "projectId": 2, "kind": "Task", "note": null }

### Daily totals
GET {{base}}/reports/daily?date=2026-11-17

### ---------------- Phase 2 ----------------

### Calendar status (source, Google connected?, last sync, errors)
GET {{base}}/calendar/status

### Sync now
POST {{base}}/calendar/sync

### Imported events for a range (counted flag, exclusion reason, meeting type, project)
GET {{base}}/calendar/events?from=2026-11-16&to=2026-11-22

### Choose the calendar source and meeting settings (Phase 1 fields are required)
PUT {{base}}/settings
Content-Type: application/json

{ "workdayStart": "08:45", "workdayEnd": "17:30", "timerWarningMinutes": 180, "timeZone": "America/New_York",
  "calendarSource": "ICal", "maxMeetingMinutes": 120, "internalDomains": "cfs.canon.com, canon.com",
  "reviewReminderEnabled": true, "reviewReminderTime": "17:15" }

### Google sign-in: open this in the browser (not via REST Client)
# http://127.0.0.1:8080/api/calendar/google/connect?origin=http://127.0.0.1:8080

### Meeting rules
GET {{base}}/meeting-rules

###
POST {{base}}/meeting-rules
Content-Type: application/json

{ "pattern": "origination|AG failover", "projectId": 2, "sortOrder": null, "active": true }

### Which project would a title get?
POST {{base}}/meeting-rules/test
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Weekly Origination sync" }

### End-of-day rollover: candidates, then roll (task 7 opted out → backlog)
GET {{base}}/tasks/rollover

###
POST {{base}}/tasks/rollover
Content-Type: application/json

{ "date": null, "skipTaskIds": [7] }

### Weekly summary (any date; snaps to Monday)
GET {{base}}/reports/weekly?start=2026-11-16

### Interruptions by source / person / weekday×hour
GET {{base}}/reports/interruptions?from=2026-11-01&to=2026-11-30

### Planned vs actual
GET {{base}}/reports/planned?from=2026-11-16&to=2026-11-22

### Daily aggregates (missing past days are computed on the fly)
GET {{base}}/aggregates?from=2026-11-01&to=2026-11-30

### Recompute aggregates after fixing old data
POST {{base}}/aggregates/recompute
Content-Type: application/json

{ "from": "2026-10-01", "to": "2026-11-30" }

### CSV export: time-entries | interruptions | calendar-events | daily-aggregates
GET {{base}}/export/time-entries.csv?from=2026-11-01&to=2026-11-30
